    31	#       exactly 3 non-bg, non-3 swatches appear there once each; the rest is bg.
    32	#   - A second full-height vertical color-3 line and one horizontal color-3 line lie on
    33	#     the divider's right side, splitting the main board into four rectangular regions.
    34	#   - Each region contains one or more disconnected black-based rectangles.
    35	#
    36	# behavior_trace:
    37	#   - Suppose the legend colors are {1, 4, 8}.
    38	#   - Region A has two disconnected objects:
    39	#       object 1 contains {0, 1}
    40	#       object 2 contains {0, 4, 8, 5}
    41	#   - Original task logic:
    42	#       object 1 does not have all targets -> keep
    43	#       object 2 has all 3 targets -> delete only object 2
    44	#   - Fused logic:
    45	#       first detect that the leftmost full-height color-3 line with a tiny 3-swatch
    46	#       strip on its left is the legend divider
    47	#       then ignore every color-3 wall and treat Region A as one bounded area
    48	#       union of Region A colors is {0, 1, 4, 5, 8} -> delete all object pixels in A
    49	#   - The key difference is visible only after both changes are combined:
    50	#       legend detection is no longer frame-based, and deletion scope is no longer
    51	#       component-based.
    52	#
    53	# complexity_calibration:
    54	#   - The legend divider orientation is fixed to vertical in generation even though the
    55	#     solver accepts horizontal separators too. This keeps examples consistent enough for
    56	#     humans while still realizing the single-line-separator idea.
    57	#   - The main board always uses one extra vertical wall plus one horizontal wall, giving
    58	#     exactly four easy-to-read regions. This is enough to make region scope observable
    59	#     without turning the board into a maze.
    60	#   - Deleted regions are built from multiple disconnected objects whose target colors are
    61	#     intentionally split, so at least one sample-level decision differs from any naive
    62	#     componentwise reading.
    63	#
    64	# old_main_assumptions_that_break:
    65	#   - _find_legend(...) from the source task assumed an L-shaped frame; that is invalid.
    66	#   - components_mask(g != bg, connectivity=4) is invalid because color 3 now appears in
    67	#     the main board as walls rather than payload.
    68	#   - Checking target coverage per connected component is invalid because the new matching
    69	#     scope is a whole separator-bounded region.
    70	#   - Treating every non-bg color as object data is invalid because color 3 is structural.
    71	#
    72	# generator_legality:
    73	#   - All walls are drawn before objects are placed.
    74	#   - Every object is placed inside one region-local canvas, so it cannot cross a wall,
    75	#     overlap another object, or leave the grid.
    76	#   - The legend side contains only bg plus exactly 3 target swatches, so the legend
    77	#     divider is uniquely detectable despite sharing color 3 with normal walls.
    78	#
    79	# visibility_and_cleanliness_checks:
    80	#   - There are always multiple color-3 lines, so the solver must distinguish roles.
    81	#   - Every region is occupied, but only deleted regions have full target coverage.
    82	#   - Deleted regions always include a region-level-only witness: their union has all
    83	#     target colors while no single object in that region has all of them.
    84	#   - No rule depends on color ordering or numeric magnitude; only explicit membership in
    85	#     the legend palette matters.
    86	#
    87	# new_solver_assumptions_and_generator_support:
    88	#   - Assumption: the legend divider is a full straight border-color line touching both
    89	#     outer borders in one axis, and the top-left side of that line contains exactly 3
    90	#     non-bg, non-border cells with no black object cells.
    91	#     Generator guarantee: the left strip below the swatches is pure bg.
    92	#   - Assumption: main objects never use color 3.
    93	#     Generator guarantee: object palettes exclude BORDER.
    94	#   - Assumption: region walls fully block 4-connectivity between neighboring regions.
    95	#     Generator guarantee: the wall network is continuous and objects are placed strictly
    96	#     inside region boxes.
